feat(tool-market): contract identity for continuous futures

Two failures happened in one day because a continuous series has no identity:

  1. CL=F rolled from CLZ26 to CLF27 on 2026-11-19 and the provider's label still
     said 'Crude Oil Dec 26'. A daily bar minted on December was quoted as support
     against a January price about 0.95 USD away — the distance was silently wrong.
  2. The splice hid the day's move: both contracts rose ~1.22%, the continuous
     series printed +0.07%, and an intraday read showed the SIGN flipped (-0.54%
     while January was +0.61%).

resolve_contract answers the question the label cannot: it prices the candidate
months, matches the continuous close against them within 0.25% (adjacent months
differ by ~1%, so this is identity, not similarity), scans 40 bars for the last day
the match changed, and reports the roll date plus the current spread.

contract.ts is pure and clock-injected: month-code generation across a year
boundary, symbol construction per venue, matching, and lastRoll which deliberately
ignores unmatched days so a missing quote cannot masquerade as a roll.

The rule the tool now states: continuous series for direction and shape, price
levels from the ACTIVE named contract.

36 test files, 572 tests.